00:13:28,775 --> 00:13:31,244
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...

230
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:33,346
...in the Hollywood Hills...

231
00:13:33,413 --> 00:13:36,749
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.

232
00:13:36,816 --> 00:13:38,751
-Oh, ba--
-Ms. Gail.

233
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:40,520
-Miss Bev has clarity.
VICTOR: Katie.

234
00:13:40,587 --> 00:13:42,489
-You see--
-Look.

235
00:13:42,555 --> 00:13:45,926
--the lowly peasant tills
the soil for 40 years
without any rain.

236
00:13:45,993 --> 00:13:49,496
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered
hydroponics...

237
00:13:49,562 --> 00:13:52,765
-...all of a sudden gets
disgusted by the--
-And see? No sense.

238
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:55,435
-That didn't make any sense.
-Let me finish. You--

239
00:13:55,502 --> 00:13:57,537
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray
all day.

240
00:13:57,604 --> 00:13:59,806
-I don't feel nothing.
-You don't have a soul.

241
00:13:59,873 --> 00:14:03,176
GAIL: No, you don't have soul.
-I have a many souls. I'll give
you one.

242
00:14:03,243 --> 00:14:07,814
-Where's your third eye? Turn
that thing on.
-I have a fourth eye too. You
wanna see it?

243
00:14:07,881 --> 00:14:10,283
-What?
-Shh.

244
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:13,887
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.

245
00:14:14,621 --> 00:14:16,356
[PIANO NOTE PLAYS]

246
00:14:16,423 --> 00:14:21,962
[SINGING OFF KEY]
Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do

247
00:14:22,029 --> 00:14:24,697
Just stop. Stop the wowing,
okay?

248
00:14:24,764 --> 00:14:26,533
BEV: What's wrong?
-Somehow you've gotten worse.

249
00:14:26,599 --> 00:14:28,668
I don't know how that was
possible...

250
00:14:28,735 --> 00:14:31,404
...but there isn't enough
Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.

251
00:14:31,471 --> 00:14:34,908
-Well, Katie's bad playing threw
me off.
-I don't think it was that.

252
00:14:34,975 --> 00:14:36,709
Again.

253
00:14:36,776 --> 00:14:38,445
Really? Okay.

254
00:14:38,511 --> 00:14:43,951
[OFF KEY]
Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do

255
00:14:44,017 --> 00:14:45,318
Ouch.

256
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:48,821
[WHISPERS]
I could belch the song better.

257
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:50,223
[BURPS]

258
00:14:50,290 --> 00:14:52,559
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?

259
00:14:52,625 --> 00:14:54,194
Anything to forget I live here.

260
00:14:54,261 --> 00:14:57,464
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.

261
00:14:57,530 --> 00:15:01,334
-Ravi, meditate me.
[WHISPERS] Good luck, buddy.

262
00:15:01,401 --> 00:15:05,472
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.

263
00:15:09,542 --> 00:15:12,012
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?

264
00:15:12,079 --> 00:15:13,913
[BELCHES]
No.

265
00:15:13,981 --> 00:15:16,416
Hmm. Nice work.

266
00:15:28,461 --> 00:15:31,864
-Guess who's on his way over.
-Not now, Victor, I'm busy.

267
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:34,534
Guess or prepare to get creamed.

268
00:15:43,043 --> 00:15:44,611
[LAUGHING]

269
00:15:44,677 --> 00:15:48,115
KATIE:
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!

270
00:15:51,784 --> 00:15:54,021
KATIE [SINGING]:
I've got rings on my fingers

271
00:15:54,087 --> 00:15:55,655
And glitter in my hair

272
00:15:55,722 --> 00:16:00,427
I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here

273
00:16:00,493 --> 00:16:01,528
I'm gonna run--

274
00:16:01,594 --> 00:16:04,998
-Ha-ha-ha.
-Victor, what are you doing?

275
00:16:05,065 --> 00:16:06,466
Victor!

276
00:16:06,533 --> 00:16:09,869
Victor, where did you put my
clothes?

277
00:16:09,936 --> 00:16:12,405
-Surprise!
-What? No.

278
00:16:12,472 --> 00:16:14,007
[KATIE SHRIEKS]

279
00:16:15,608 --> 00:16:17,544
KATIE:
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!

280
00:16:17,610 --> 00:16:18,678
[VICTOR LAUGHS]

281
00:16:24,617 --> 00:16:26,153
[GRUMBLES]

282
00:16:27,154 --> 00:16:28,621
Oh, hi, Katie.

283
00:16:28,688 --> 00:16:29,989
You are evil. Let me in.

284
00:16:30,057 --> 00:16:33,793
I control every lock on this
property.

285
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:35,462
Crap.

286
00:16:38,731 --> 00:16:40,533
This is insane.

287
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:45,004
Yeah, try the shed, it's
unlocked, idiot.

288
00:16:53,446 --> 00:16:54,581
[SIGHS]

289
00:16:54,647 --> 00:16:56,849
You gotta be kidding me.

290
00:16:56,916 --> 00:16:58,418
[GASPS]

291
00:16:58,485 --> 00:17:00,120
Crap.

292
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:06,793
How did such an untalented
daughter
spring from my loins?

293
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:10,963
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal
deity.

294
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,266
Tell him to give me fame and
fortune.

295
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:15,135
Not exactly how it works.

296
00:17:15,202 --> 00:17:17,670
Now, breathe through your Mula
Bandha.

297
00:17:17,737 --> 00:17:20,907
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on
YouTube.

298
00:17:20,973 --> 00:17:23,510
How much longer is this gonna
take?
Ugh.

299
00:17:23,576 --> 00:17:26,045
The prayer or the fame and
fortune?

300
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:29,649
Ha, ha. See you later.

301
00:17:35,888 --> 00:17:37,690
Victor.

302
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:42,762
LUKE:
Katie?

303
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:46,399
-Luke.
-Katie.

304
00:17:46,466 --> 00:17:49,836
-Are you wearing a doormat?
-Yes.

305
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:52,805
-Welcome.
-Why, thank you.

306
00:17:53,906 --> 00:17:55,375
The truth. Um....

307
00:17:56,643 --> 00:18:00,547
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.

308
00:18:00,613 --> 00:18:02,715
Naked.

309
00:18:02,782 --> 00:18:05,185
Oh, sorry. You should--
You should take my jacket.

310
00:18:05,252 --> 00:18:07,120
KATIE: Oh.
-Oh, no, no.

311
00:18:09,222 --> 00:18:10,423
There.

312
00:18:10,490 --> 00:18:13,826
-Thanks. Now the pants.
-Hmm?

313
00:18:18,298 --> 00:18:20,400
I'm kidding.

314
00:18:20,467 --> 00:18:21,834
-You got me.
-Ha, ha.

315
00:18:21,901 --> 00:18:23,670
No, no.

316
00:18:23,736 --> 00:18:27,340
One more parent-teacher
conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.

317
00:18:27,407 --> 00:18:29,942
Look at me. I'm an educator.

318
00:18:30,009 --> 00:18:35,114
I have no real skills. And I
will die
before I go back to my daddy's
farm.

319
00:18:35,182 --> 00:18:39,286
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan.
Do it.

320
00:18:39,352 --> 00:18:41,888
I'll put another banana on the
altar.

321
00:18:43,089 --> 00:18:45,958
[ANGELIC CHOIR SINGING NEARBY]

322
00:18:46,025 --> 00:18:47,994
What is that?

323
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:50,430
Do you hear angels singing?

324
00:18:50,497 --> 00:18:52,599
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.

325
00:18:53,866 --> 00:18:55,535
Hey. What--?

326
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:58,671
[DOORBELL RINGS]

327
00:19:03,676 --> 00:19:05,912
[ANGELIC CHOIR SINGING
ON CELL PHONE]

328
00:19:08,114 --> 00:19:10,917
-This is Gail Van Ravensway.
GUY [ON PHONE]: Hello.

329
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:12,919
Guy Morgan here. How are you?

330
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,821
Oh, well, hello, Guy.

331
00:19:14,887 --> 00:19:17,224
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.

332
00:19:17,290 --> 00:19:18,658
Do you hear this?

333
00:19:18,725 --> 00:19:20,493
[KATIE SINGING ON STEREO]
I can justify

334
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:22,362
That's the demo your girl,
Katie...

335
00:19:22,429 --> 00:19:24,864
...slipped into my briefcase.

336
00:19:24,931 --> 00:19:27,234
And it sounds like money, dear.

337
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,269
She gave you a CD?

338
00:19:29,336 --> 00:19:32,639
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the
berries.

339
00:19:33,740 --> 00:19:36,576
Ravi, what frigging god did you
pray to?

340
00:19:38,845 --> 00:19:43,250
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.

341
00:19:43,316 --> 00:19:45,051
[DOORBELL RINGING]

342
00:19:45,117 --> 00:19:47,454
Katie, somebody get that door!

343
00:19:48,655 --> 00:19:51,023
So...

344
00:19:51,090 --> 00:19:52,925
...that meeting today...

345
00:19:52,992 --> 00:19:56,263
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.

346
00:19:56,329 --> 00:19:58,498
He's an idiot for not liking
your music.

347
00:19:58,565 --> 00:20:01,200
Well, it's-- It's complicated.

348
00:20:01,268 --> 00:20:02,769
I'm gonna just, uh....

349
00:20:02,835 --> 00:20:03,670
[DOORBELL RINGS]

350
00:20:03,736 --> 00:20:05,738
Is it as complicated as me...

351
00:20:05,805 --> 00:20:09,342
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?

352
00:20:09,409 --> 00:20:13,280
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.

353
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,249
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

354
00:20:16,316 --> 00:20:17,984
[DOOR OPENS]

355
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:20,753
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?

356
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:23,990
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal
Mini-Me.

357
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:26,659
Oh, I know, tell me about it.
Come on in.

358
00:20:30,497 --> 00:20:32,299
Oh, my God, did you work out
today?

359
00:20:33,833 --> 00:20:35,234
-Sit down.
-Ooh, look at this.

360
00:20:35,302 --> 00:20:38,505
-Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
-Why, thank you.

361
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:40,940
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...

362
00:20:41,007 --> 00:20:43,109
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.

363
00:20:43,175 --> 00:20:44,844
That's interesting.

364
00:20:44,911 --> 00:20:47,980
-She's absolutely lovely--
-Would you like an appetizer?

365
00:20:48,047 --> 00:20:49,181
Oh, fromage.

366
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:51,017
I only have cheese.

367
00:20:53,853 --> 00:20:56,122
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.

368
00:20:56,188 --> 00:20:58,024
Your phone.

369
00:21:00,927 --> 00:21:04,163
He just loved that little demo
you left him.

370
00:21:04,230 --> 00:21:05,865
I have underestimated you.

371
00:21:05,932 --> 00:21:08,100
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.

372
00:21:08,167 --> 00:21:11,471
-I didn't lie about anything.
-Oh, but, chicken, you did.

373
00:21:11,538 --> 00:21:13,906
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.

374
00:21:13,973 --> 00:21:18,345
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.

375
00:21:18,411 --> 00:21:21,981
-But you can't do that. That's
my song.
-It's Bev's song.

376
00:21:22,048 --> 00:21:25,485
And Guy can't wait to see her
perform it
at the Showcase.

377
00:21:25,552 --> 00:21:28,888
If you try to contact him, I'll
deny
everything and lock you in the
basement.

378
00:21:28,955 --> 00:21:34,293
-She can't sing to save her
life.
-No, but you can, can't you?

379
00:21:35,562 --> 00:21:37,864
Now, let's hear this amazing
voice.

380
00:21:41,233 --> 00:21:42,869
[PLAYING GUITAR AND SINGING]

381
00:21:42,935 --> 00:21:47,306
Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor

382
00:21:47,374 --> 00:21:51,944
Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her

383
00:21:52,011 --> 00:21:56,383
She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi--

384
00:21:56,449 --> 00:21:58,217
Well, your lyrics stink.

385
00:21:58,284 --> 00:22:00,620
But Guy's right, you've got
chops.

386
00:22:00,687 --> 00:22:02,021
[LUKE PLAYING PIANO]

387
00:22:02,088 --> 00:22:03,690
[BEV SMASHES KEYS]

388
00:22:03,756 --> 00:22:06,959
Do you know what other
instruments
I'm good at?

389
00:22:07,026 --> 00:22:11,063
I have a feeling I could get in
trouble
with a question like that.

390
00:22:11,130 --> 00:22:13,032
I like trouble.

391
00:22:14,434 --> 00:22:16,803
GAIL:
Hey, kids.

392
00:22:16,869 --> 00:22:20,206
-Good evening, Miss Van
Ravensway.
-Sorry, I need you to go. Now.

393
00:22:20,272 --> 00:22:23,242
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.

394
00:22:23,309 --> 00:22:27,279
-So she had a lovely evening.
Ta-ta.
-Are you trying to ruin my life?

395
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:32,719
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the
Showcase.

396
00:22:32,785 --> 00:22:35,221
-So you do think I've improved?
-Oh, no, honey.

397
00:22:35,287 --> 00:22:37,957
But my month of spiritual
devotion
has taught me...

398
00:22:38,024 --> 00:22:40,693
...that God works in annoying
ways.

399
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:43,463
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?

400
00:22:43,530 --> 00:22:46,499
You can't, but Katie can.

401
00:22:46,566 --> 00:22:49,569
-What?
-I know. Like I said, annoying.

402
00:22:49,636 --> 00:22:53,039
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.

403
00:22:53,105 --> 00:22:55,775
What if I don't want to?

404
00:22:55,842 --> 00:22:59,746
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.

405
00:22:59,812 --> 00:23:01,914
-I saved your life.
-You didn't do anything.

406
00:23:01,981 --> 00:23:04,417
-My dad married you.
-Yeah, and then he died.

407
00:23:04,484 --> 00:23:08,354
I tried to put you in foster
care,
but they was all fulled up on
ugly.

408
00:23:08,421 --> 00:23:09,856
-Funny.
-I thought it was...

409
00:23:09,922 --> 00:23:11,691
...because you don't wanna look
bad.

410
00:23:13,159 --> 00:23:15,194
Katie, if you don't sing...

411
00:23:15,261 --> 00:23:18,531
...I'm gonna find a way for that
savings
your dad left to disappear.

412
00:23:18,598 --> 00:23:23,102
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here
with me.

413
00:23:23,169 --> 00:23:27,106
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old
together.

414
00:23:27,173 --> 00:23:30,376
Why don't you just have her
perform
if you like her so much?

415
00:23:30,443 --> 00:23:32,812
Because, honey, look at you.

416
00:23:32,879 --> 00:23:34,914
You are a star.

417
00:23:34,981 --> 00:23:39,486
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.

418
00:23:39,552 --> 00:23:41,020
I'm a star.

419
00:23:41,087 --> 00:23:45,558
-A bright, gassy star.
-Yes, you are.

420
00:23:45,625 --> 00:23:48,461
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...

421
00:23:48,528 --> 00:23:49,662
...shaped just like Colin
Farrell.

422
00:23:49,729 --> 00:23:51,631
Every part of him.

423
00:23:51,698 --> 00:23:55,702
Or, Bev, you could just see
every part of Colin Farrell
on the Internet.

424
00:23:55,768 --> 00:23:58,137
And just leave me out of this.

425
00:23:59,806 --> 00:24:02,542
-Okay, so how do we do this?
-First rule of Lie Club...

426
00:24:02,609 --> 00:24:04,844
...is don't talk about Lie Club.

427
00:24:04,911 --> 00:24:06,913
Which includes you, Katie.

428
00:24:06,979 --> 00:24:09,782
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.

429
00:24:09,849 --> 00:24:12,218
And no more talking to Luke or
Guy.

430
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:14,020
Are we clear?

431
00:24:14,086 --> 00:24:15,254
Crystal.

432
00:24:15,321 --> 00:24:16,956
[BELL TOLLING]

433
00:24:17,023 --> 00:24:19,926
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.

434
00:24:19,992 --> 00:24:24,296
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.

435
00:24:24,363 --> 00:24:27,133
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.

436
00:24:27,199 --> 00:24:28,668
Yeah. Okay.

437
00:24:28,735 --> 00:24:30,436
-Yeah, okay. Bye.
-Dude, what'd he say?

438
00:24:30,503 --> 00:24:32,438
These guys you
told me about are good?

439
00:24:32,505 --> 00:24:35,975
Yes. The Oral Majority has
potential.
They'll be here any second.

440
00:24:36,042 --> 00:24:38,811
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with
Bev?

441
00:24:38,878 --> 00:24:41,480
-Her mom kicked me out.
-I told you. Bev is drama.

442
00:24:41,548 --> 00:24:43,015
Technically, it was Gail's
drama.

443
00:24:43,082 --> 00:24:45,317
But Bev's interesting, man.
She's--

444
00:24:45,384 --> 00:24:46,953
I'm worried she's bonkers.

445
00:24:47,019 --> 00:24:49,956
See, my last girlfriend, she was
hot, but absolutely mental.

446
00:24:50,022 --> 00:24:52,792
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.

447
00:24:52,859 --> 00:24:54,727
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the
facilities.

448
00:24:54,794 --> 00:24:56,863
Facilities. That's a new one.

449
00:24:56,929 --> 00:24:59,599
-Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
-Hey, what's good, y'all?

450
00:24:59,666 --> 00:25:02,702
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the
facilities.

451
00:25:02,769 --> 00:25:04,270
We're here to impress.

452
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:06,739
-Clear, right?
-Got it.

453
00:25:10,242 --> 00:25:12,812
[SINGING]
When you're fighting just to
keep it sane

454
00:25:12,879 --> 00:25:15,247
Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane

455
00:25:15,314 --> 00:25:17,817
-Sing it out
-Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh

456
00:25:17,884 --> 00:25:21,153
-Help me sing it out
-Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh

457
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:23,856
If you wanna find out who you
are
Stop running

458
00:25:23,923 --> 00:25:27,293
In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing

459
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:32,765
All night, it's gonna be all
right
Hey, hey, hey, hey

460
00:25:32,832 --> 00:25:36,936
All right
Turn your dreams into your life

461
00:25:40,773 --> 00:25:42,609
That's good.

462
00:25:49,315 --> 00:25:53,586
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.

463
00:25:53,653 --> 00:25:56,088
Oh, Katie, baby, your life
sucks.

464
00:25:56,155 --> 00:25:58,625
Trust me, it gets worse.

465
00:25:58,691 --> 00:26:03,262
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in
there--

466
00:26:03,329 --> 00:26:04,764
-I was trying to hold them
back--
-You're right.

467
00:26:04,831 --> 00:26:06,933
They have potential and they're
great.

468
00:26:06,999 --> 00:26:12,538
But first, my talent-finding
friend,
promise me no more auditions in
the bogs.

469
00:26:12,605 --> 00:26:15,374
-The what?
-The loo.

470
00:26:15,441 --> 00:26:16,943
-Bathroom. Toilet.
-Got it.

471
00:26:17,009 --> 00:26:20,613
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.

472
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:23,883
So now I have to rehearse in
secret.

473
00:26:23,950 --> 00:26:25,184
Why not not rehearse?

474
00:26:25,251 --> 00:26:27,787
Make Bev sound bad. What do you
care?

475
00:26:27,854 --> 00:26:31,390
No song, no savings account. No
life.

476
00:26:31,457 --> 00:26:32,892
[CHATTERING AND LAUGHING]

477
00:26:32,959 --> 00:26:35,728
ANGELA:
People. Coming. Now.

478
00:26:39,131 --> 00:26:41,267
Okay.

479
00:26:41,333 --> 00:26:43,836
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.

480
00:26:43,903 --> 00:26:45,905
LUKE:
Can you grab the mike?

481
00:26:45,972 --> 00:26:48,140
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?

482
00:26:48,207 --> 00:26:50,076
LUKE:
Dude, with bromance, comes a
fine line.

483
00:26:50,142 --> 00:26:52,845
MICKEY:
That I shall not cross.

484
00:26:52,912 --> 00:26:55,347
So sing something.

485
00:26:56,883 --> 00:26:59,151
LUKE:
Okay.

486
00:26:59,218 --> 00:27:02,354
[PLAYING UPBEAT MELODY]

487
00:27:02,421 --> 00:27:05,124
[SINGING] I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain

488
00:27:05,191 --> 00:27:07,694
I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made

489
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:09,929
Oh, oh

490
00:27:09,996 --> 00:27:12,131
Whoa, oh, oh, oh

491
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:16,302
My soul's in debt, but my bills
are paid

492
00:27:16,368 --> 00:27:19,005
I'd give anything just to make
an escape

493
00:27:19,071 --> 00:27:21,207
Oh, oh

494
00:27:21,273 --> 00:27:23,810
Whoa, oh, oh, oh

495
00:27:23,876 --> 00:27:26,713
So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking

496
00:27:26,779 --> 00:27:29,615
Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever
letting you in

497
00:27:29,682 --> 00:27:31,083
[MOUTHS]
He's amazing.

498
00:27:32,551 --> 00:27:34,887
Not again

499
00:27:34,954 --> 00:27:37,690
So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking

500
00:27:37,757 --> 00:27:43,462
But, baby, you're better off
walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in

501
00:27:43,529 --> 00:27:45,031
Never again

502
00:27:45,998 --> 00:27:48,901
I went out on a limb again

503
00:27:48,968 --> 00:27:51,437
I guess I had to lose to win

504
00:27:51,503 --> 00:27:55,641
I was too confused to know
Which way to turn

505
00:27:55,708 --> 00:27:57,276
[CELL PHONE BEEPS]

506
00:27:57,343 --> 00:28:00,112
-And she could be a
millionaire....
-Crap.

507
00:28:00,179 --> 00:28:02,749
-Gail needs me to drive her
home.
-I don't care

508
00:28:02,815 --> 00:28:05,584
'Cause, baby, there's nobody
home

509
00:28:05,651 --> 00:28:08,087
Nobody's home at all, yeah

510
00:28:11,423 --> 00:28:12,558
[MICKEY LAUGHS]

511
00:28:12,624 --> 00:28:14,861
-What? Did you write that?
-Yeah.

512
00:28:14,927 --> 00:28:17,263
Reminds me of, um.... Uh....

513
00:28:17,329 --> 00:28:21,067
-Danger Fruit, right? Danger
Fruit.
-Ha, ha. Because I wrote their
album too.

514
00:28:21,133 --> 00:28:23,936
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.

515
00:28:24,003 --> 00:28:25,905
-I love that album. That's
crazy.
-Yeah.

516
00:28:25,972 --> 00:28:27,907
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...

517
00:28:27,974 --> 00:28:30,342
...was a pile of crap.

518
00:28:30,409 --> 00:28:32,478
He thinks writing's a waste of
time.

519
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:36,783
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better
hair.

520
00:28:36,849 --> 00:28:40,853
But the first thing I thought
when
I heard those guys in the
urinals was...

521
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:42,488
...good acoustics.

522
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:46,692
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.

523
00:28:46,759 --> 00:28:48,294
If you gave them your song.

524
00:28:49,762 --> 00:28:51,730
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.

525
00:28:51,798 --> 00:28:54,266
-So put them in the Showcase?
-Put them in the Showcase.

526
00:28:54,333 --> 00:28:55,935
MICKEY:
Yeah.

527
00:28:56,002 --> 00:28:57,369
[KATIE PLAYING GUITAR AND
SINGING]

528
00:28:57,436 --> 00:29:03,575
You can never tell where this
might go

529
00:29:03,642 --> 00:29:05,845
You wrote that song today?

530
00:29:05,912 --> 00:29:09,481
-You've been home for what,
two hours?
-It's like an answer to his
song.

531
00:29:09,548 --> 00:29:10,950
You really like this guy.

532
00:29:11,017 --> 00:29:12,819
Yeah, I'm an idiot.

533
00:29:12,885 --> 00:29:15,187
You have to sing that for him.

534
00:29:15,254 --> 00:29:18,891
What if you sang to him in
secret?

535
00:29:20,559 --> 00:29:23,495
At the dance. Ta-da.

536
00:29:26,966 --> 00:29:29,936
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but....

537
00:29:31,838 --> 00:29:34,373
Oh, God, I hope you like it.

538
00:29:34,440 --> 00:29:38,444
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?

539
00:29:38,510 --> 00:29:40,279
No, I know you're crazy.

540
00:29:40,346 --> 00:29:42,314
Am not.

541
00:29:42,381 --> 00:29:45,751
-What if he doesn't even like
me?
-You'll both be in disguise.

542
00:29:45,818 --> 00:29:48,354
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with
you.

543
00:29:48,420 --> 00:29:51,290
I was naked. Of course he was
flirting.

544
00:29:51,357 --> 00:29:53,792
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.

545
00:29:53,860 --> 00:29:56,062
Why not? Tell him how you feel.

546
00:29:56,128 --> 00:30:00,466
If he feels the same way, you
can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell
Gail.

547
00:30:00,532 --> 00:30:03,970
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.

548
00:30:06,772 --> 00:30:08,540
Okay.

549
00:30:08,607 --> 00:30:10,409
I'm going to the dance.

550
00:30:10,476 --> 00:30:11,710
That's my girl.

551
00:30:11,777 --> 00:30:15,882
Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.

552
00:30:15,948 --> 00:30:19,551
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were
you.

553
00:30:19,618 --> 00:30:21,687
What? Why?

554
00:30:21,753 --> 00:30:23,055
Hey. Wake up.

555
00:30:26,825 --> 00:30:28,494
GAIL:
Katie!

556
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:32,298
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.

557
00:30:32,364 --> 00:30:33,765
Go.

558
00:30:33,832 --> 00:30:35,667
I told you we don't have a cat.

559
00:30:35,734 --> 00:30:37,203
Angie, heads up.

560
00:30:39,238 --> 00:30:40,472
Katie!

561
00:30:45,744 --> 00:30:47,579
What's going on?

562
00:30:47,646 --> 00:30:48,981
Nothing.

563
00:30:49,048 --> 00:30:52,084
I am, uh, re-organizing and
labeling. I....

564
00:30:52,151 --> 00:30:54,820
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?

565
00:30:54,887 --> 00:30:59,025
I would make you a sweater, but
I hear
that the arms, that they're
really hard.

566
00:31:01,928 --> 00:31:06,465
Oh, you thought you could sneak
off
and go to the dance.

567
00:31:06,532 --> 00:31:08,867
After what you pulled today with
Guy.

568
00:31:08,935 --> 00:31:10,669
Oh, no, no.

569
00:31:10,736 --> 00:31:13,139
Oh, no, no, no.

570
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:15,407
You're on Victor watch
tonight...

571
00:31:15,474 --> 00:31:18,177
...tomorrow night and every
night.

572
00:31:18,244 --> 00:31:19,778
Fun.

573
00:31:19,845 --> 00:31:22,982
I'll give Victor all the
mothering you don't have
time for.

574
00:31:23,049 --> 00:31:27,253
Oh, I wish you could be my
mommy.

575
00:31:27,319 --> 00:31:30,022
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.

576
00:31:30,089 --> 00:31:33,259
[HIP-HOP MUSIC PLAYING ON
STEREO]

577
00:31:33,325 --> 00:31:35,962
KATIE: Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.

578
00:31:36,028 --> 00:31:38,730
Or worse, the furniture.

579
00:31:38,797 --> 00:31:41,700
ANGELA: Hello?
-Hey.

580
00:31:41,767 --> 00:31:45,404
-You look like you're having
fun.
-Always.

581
00:31:45,471 --> 00:31:48,440
Well, I couldn't let you not go
to the dance
without me.

582
00:31:48,507 --> 00:31:51,210
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.

583
00:31:51,277 --> 00:31:54,313
So let's just get this party
started.

584
00:31:54,380 --> 00:31:58,217
-So is Victor driving you nuts?
-I swear to you, he's not human.

585
00:31:58,284 --> 00:32:02,188
I mean, can you really blame
him, though?
Just look at this family.

586
00:32:03,255 --> 00:32:04,656
Victor, what are you doing?

587
00:32:04,723 --> 00:32:06,658
[YELLS]

588
00:32:11,998 --> 00:32:13,299
[LAUGHS]

589
00:32:14,733 --> 00:32:16,902
Oh, no. Great.

590
00:32:16,969 --> 00:32:19,705
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.

591
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:21,940
KATIE:
True. Ugh. Whatever.

592
00:32:23,775 --> 00:32:27,613
Why did I ever think that
tonight
could've been something special.

593
00:32:27,679 --> 00:32:30,249
Think Bev's all over Luke at the
dance
right now?

594
00:32:30,316 --> 00:32:32,518
They're probably making out.
See?

595
00:32:32,584 --> 00:32:36,122
-Victor, give it a rest.
-Just check it out. Come on.

596
00:32:38,991 --> 00:32:41,927
Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.

597
00:32:41,994 --> 00:32:44,963
So we need a little insurance.

598
00:32:45,031 --> 00:32:49,268
-I know what I'm doing, Mother.
GAIL: Do you?

599
00:32:49,335 --> 00:32:52,304
I can't take it anymore, okay?

600
00:32:52,371 --> 00:32:54,740
I'm taking my life into my own
hands.

601
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:56,242
I'm talking to Luke.

602
00:32:56,308 --> 00:32:58,910
-Finally.
-Okay, but we have gotta be
home...

603
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:01,180
...before Gail gets here.

604
00:33:01,247 --> 00:33:02,681
What about the demon spawn?

605
00:33:02,748 --> 00:33:03,882
Mm-hm.

606
00:33:03,949 --> 00:33:05,484
KATIE:
Right.

607
00:33:06,352 --> 00:33:07,686
Okay, just watch him.

608
00:33:10,822 --> 00:33:12,224
ANGELA:
Hmm.

609
00:33:14,693 --> 00:33:15,627
[BARKS]

610
00:33:15,694 --> 00:33:16,695
[CHUCKLES]

611
00:33:16,762 --> 00:33:19,065
Is that all you've got, Angela?

612
00:33:19,131 --> 00:33:20,299
Ravi?

613
00:33:20,366 --> 00:33:22,000
[SPORTS COMMENTATORS
TALKING ON TV]

614
00:33:22,068 --> 00:33:24,903
RAVI [IN JERSEY ACCENT]:
My sister could catch that,
jerknut.

615
00:33:24,970 --> 00:33:27,539
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.

616
00:33:29,541 --> 00:33:32,010
[IN INDIAN ACCENT]
Miss Katie, I am most startled.

617
00:33:32,078 --> 00:33:33,745
Obviously.

618
00:33:33,812 --> 00:33:36,815
[IN JERSEY ACCENT]
All right. All right. Don't hate
me.

619
00:33:36,882 --> 00:33:38,350
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.

620
00:33:38,417 --> 00:33:42,254
But my name ain't Ravi. It's
Tony.

621
00:33:42,321 --> 00:33:45,557
-Tony.
-Tony Gupta from Jersey.

622
00:33:45,624 --> 00:33:48,594
-From Jersey.
-I am half Indian.

623
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:52,164
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.

624
00:33:52,231 --> 00:33:54,333
Truth is I always wanted to be
an actor.

625
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:55,901
But I never got my shot.

626
00:33:55,967 --> 00:33:58,504
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...

627
00:33:58,570 --> 00:34:01,140
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"

628
00:34:01,207 --> 00:34:03,041
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:

629
00:34:03,109 --> 00:34:05,211
[IN INDIAN ACCENT]
"Who is asking?"

630
00:34:05,277 --> 00:34:08,614
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
She says, "Someone who's paying
for some spiritual guidance."

631
00:34:08,680 --> 00:34:11,583
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a
miracle!"

632
00:34:11,650 --> 00:34:16,255
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a
character.

633
00:34:16,322 --> 00:34:18,890
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?

634
00:34:18,957 --> 00:34:21,727
Ravi is my King Lear.

635
00:34:21,793 --> 00:34:24,230
[IN ENGLISH ACCENT]
You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?

636
00:34:24,296 --> 00:34:25,631
-Oy, mate.
-No, thanks.

637
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:29,701
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.

638
00:34:29,768 --> 00:34:31,937
[KATIE CHUCKLES]

639
00:34:32,003 --> 00:34:36,475
Your secret's safe with me,
okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.

640
00:34:36,542 --> 00:34:38,710
-Meatball.
-Ha, Meatball.

641
00:34:38,777 --> 00:34:41,347
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?

642
00:34:41,413 --> 00:34:42,781
Are you kidding me? Done.

643
00:34:42,848 --> 00:34:43,982
[SIGHS]

644
00:34:44,049 --> 00:34:45,684
Blow it up.

645
00:34:45,751 --> 00:34:47,453
[MIMICS EXPLOSION]

646
00:34:47,519 --> 00:34:49,755
Thank you.

647
00:34:49,821 --> 00:34:51,257
[CHUCKLES]

648
00:34:55,761 --> 00:34:58,597
[INDIAN DANCE MUSIC
PLAYING ON SPEAKERS]

649
00:34:58,664 --> 00:35:00,098
ANGELA:
Whoa.

650
00:35:00,166 --> 00:35:02,701
KATIE: How am I supposed to find
Luke if everybody's got a mask?

651
00:35:02,768 --> 00:35:06,205
ANGELA: I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some
recon.

652
00:35:06,272 --> 00:35:07,506
[CLEARS THROAT]

653
00:35:07,573 --> 00:35:10,008
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.

654
00:35:10,075 --> 00:35:13,445
No drinking. No texting. No
kissing.

655
00:35:16,014 --> 00:35:18,884
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?

656
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:23,622
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any
kind.

657
00:35:23,689 --> 00:35:26,158
Luke? Ugh.

658
00:35:29,995 --> 00:35:31,129
[KATIE SIGHS]

659
00:35:31,197 --> 00:35:33,565
Where is he?

660
00:35:33,632 --> 00:35:36,368
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to
listen to.

661
00:35:36,435 --> 00:35:38,003
-Now?
-No time like it.

662
00:35:38,069 --> 00:35:40,839
-Dude, not again--
-We're called Big Pain Ticket.

663
00:35:41,907 --> 00:35:44,142
[CHAIN SAW REVVING]

664
00:35:44,210 --> 00:35:47,879
I wanna kiss your apocalypse

665
00:35:47,946 --> 00:35:51,383
Wrap you in my Armageddon

666
00:35:51,450 --> 00:35:53,785
Sing you a twisted serenade

667
00:35:53,852 --> 00:35:56,688
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.

668
00:35:56,755 --> 00:35:59,325
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.

669
00:36:06,064 --> 00:36:07,233
I think I found him.

670
00:36:07,299 --> 00:36:09,701
ANGELA:
Well, he is blond.

671
00:36:12,671 --> 00:36:14,906
Oh, my God, what is she doing
here?

672
00:36:17,075 --> 00:36:19,278
I hate teenage desperation.

673
00:36:19,345 --> 00:36:20,846
What are you doing here?

674
00:36:20,912 --> 00:36:23,782
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...

675
00:36:23,849 --> 00:36:25,851
...by covering up its third best
asset.

676
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:29,154
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a
pig?

677
00:36:29,221 --> 00:36:30,956
Honey, I saw you making sweet
love...

678
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:33,825
...to a plate of Swedish
meatballs
at the snack table.

679
00:36:36,094 --> 00:36:38,364
It's now or never, babe.

680
00:36:39,765 --> 00:36:43,335
-What if she recognizes me?
-I'll distract her. Go.

681
00:36:43,402 --> 00:36:45,704
-So was I right or was I right?
-You were right.

682
00:36:45,771 --> 00:36:48,940
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the
men's...

683
00:36:49,007 --> 00:36:50,876
...and you're fired.

684
00:36:53,779 --> 00:36:57,449
-I know your secret.
-Which secret is that?

685
00:37:00,118 --> 00:37:01,853
I heard you sing at school.

686
00:37:01,920 --> 00:37:02,954
You were amazing.

687
00:37:03,021 --> 00:37:04,222
Do I know you?

688
00:37:08,427 --> 00:37:10,962
-I wanna show you something.
-What's your name?

689
00:37:13,365 --> 00:37:16,001
Angela, what are you doing?

690
00:37:16,067 --> 00:37:18,704
I'd like to make a request.

691
00:37:22,874 --> 00:37:26,011
I will make your night. I
promise.

692
00:37:26,077 --> 00:37:27,813
ANGELA:
Miss Van R.

693
00:37:27,879 --> 00:37:30,416
Is it true you wanted to be a
dancer
when you were younger...

694
00:37:30,482 --> 00:37:31,717
...but were never good enough?

695
00:37:31,783 --> 00:37:32,384
[SCOFFS]

696
00:37:32,451 --> 00:37:35,020
Who told you that?

697
00:37:37,689 --> 00:37:39,791
[PLAYING UPBEAT
INDIAN DANCE MUSIC]

698
00:37:47,032 --> 00:37:48,867
[PEOPLE CHEERING]

699
00:37:52,304 --> 00:37:53,939
GAIL:
Well, now, how lovely.

700
00:37:54,005 --> 00:37:57,075
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.

701
00:37:57,142 --> 00:37:58,910
CROWD:
Oh!

702
00:37:58,977 --> 00:38:03,315
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you
to a dance battle.

703
00:38:03,382 --> 00:38:05,851
